IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `cbca-core`
IMPORT `cb5-nouns`

-- Canada Business Corporations Act (R.S.C. 1985, c. C-44), PART XIX.1 -- APPORTIONING AWARD OF DAMAGES
-- (ss 237.1 to 237.9). Layer 1: the law, objectively. Nothing here takes anyone's point of view.
--
-- UNOFFICIAL. The text this was encoded from is a plain-text rendering of the Department of Justice
-- Canada consolidation current to 2026-09-30 (last amended 2026-03-26); it is not an official version,
-- and nothing here has been verified against the official text. Contains information licensed under
-- the Open Government Licence - Canada.
--
-- HOW THIS MODULE READS THE TEXT.
--   * Money is a NUMBER of Canadian dollars; a fraction is a NUMBER from 0 to 1 (the Act's "percentage
--     that corresponds to the degree of responsibility" is such a fraction).
--   * The "prescribed amount" of s 237.5(1)(b) and s 237.6(1) is fixed by the regulations, which are not
--     among the sources: it is a plain input in dollars and no figure is invented.
--   * Whether the part applies to a given proceeding also depends on the transitional section 233 of
--     S.C. 2001, c. 14 (a Related Provision at src:3577). That is in cb5-related-provisions.l4, which
--     composes it with the rules for s 237.2 here.
--   * A judgment the Act hands to the court ("the court considers that it is just and reasonable", "as
--     determined by the court") is a plain BOOLEAN or DATE input named for the judgment.

§ `Part XIX.1 -- Apportioning award of damages`

§§ `s 237.1 -- definitions`

-- "Financial interest ... includes" ten kinds. "Includes" is not "means": a thing outside the list can
-- still be a financial interest in the ordinary sense of the words, so that is a plain input beside the
-- list. Two of the kinds carry a condition of their own: (h) excludes a contract issued by an insurance
-- company governed by an Act of Parliament or a law of a province, and (j) is whatever the regulations
-- prescribe.
-- src:2939 | financial interest, with respect to a corporation, includes
-- src:2940 | (a) a security;
-- src:2941 | (b) a title to or an interest in capital, assets, property, profits, earnings or royalties;
-- src:2942 | (c) an option or other interest in, or a subscription to, a security;
-- src:2943 | (d) an agreement under which the interest of the purchaser is valued for purposes of conversion or surrender by reference to the value of a proportionate interest in a specified portfolio of assets;
-- src:2944 | (e) an agreement providing that money received will be repaid or treated as a subscription for shares, units or interests at the option of any person or the corporation;
-- src:2945 | (f) a profit-sharing agreement or certificate;
-- src:2946 | (g) a lease, claim or royalty in oil, natural gas or mining, or an interest in the lease, claim or royalty;
-- src:2947 | (h) an income or annuity contract that is not issued by an insurance company governed by an Act of Parliament or a law of a province;
-- src:2948 | (i) an investment contract; and
-- src:2949 | (j) anything that is prescribed to be a financial interest. (intérêt financier)
@ref CBCA s 237.1 "financial interest" (src:2939-2949)
DECLARE `Kind of financial interest (s 237.1)` IS ONE OF
    `a security (s 237.1 "financial interest" (a))`
    `a title to or an interest in capital, assets, property, profits, earnings or royalties (s 237.1 "financial interest" (b))`
    `an option or other interest in, or a subscription to, a security (s 237.1 "financial interest" (c))`
    `an agreement valuing the purchaser's interest by reference to a proportionate interest in a specified portfolio of assets (s 237.1 "financial interest" (d))`
    `an agreement that money received will be repaid or treated as a subscription at the option of any person or the corporation (s 237.1 "financial interest" (e))`
    `a profit-sharing agreement or certificate (s 237.1 "financial interest" (f))`
    `a lease, claim or royalty in oil, natural gas or mining, or an interest in it (s 237.1 "financial interest" (g))`
    `an income or annuity contract (s 237.1 "financial interest" (h))`
    `an investment contract (s 237.1 "financial interest" (i))`
    `anything prescribed to be a financial interest (s 237.1 "financial interest" (j))`
    `none of these kinds of financial interest (s 237.1)`

-- src:2939 | financial interest, with respect to a corporation, includes
-- src:2940 | (a) a security;
-- src:2941 | (b) a title to or an interest in capital, assets, property, profits, earnings or royalties;
-- src:2942 | (c) an option or other interest in, or a subscription to, a security;
-- src:2943 | (d) an agreement under which the interest of the purchaser is valued for purposes of conversion or surrender by reference to the value of a proportionate interest in a specified portfolio of assets;
-- src:2944 | (e) an agreement providing that money received will be repaid or treated as a subscription for shares, units or interests at the option of any person or the corporation;
-- src:2945 | (f) a profit-sharing agreement or certificate;
-- src:2946 | (g) a lease, claim or royalty in oil, natural gas or mining, or an interest in the lease, claim or royalty;
-- src:2947 | (h) an income or annuity contract that is not issued by an insurance company governed by an Act of Parliament or a law of a province;
-- src:2948 | (i) an investment contract; and
-- src:2949 | (j) anything that is prescribed to be a financial interest. (intérêt financier)
@ref CBCA s 237.1 "financial interest" (src:2939-2949)
GIVEN kind IS A `Kind of financial interest (s 237.1)`
      `it is a financial interest in the ordinary meaning of the words` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the income or annuity contract was issued by an insurance company governed by an Act of Parliament or a law of a province` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is prescribed by the regulations to be a financial interest` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `financial interest within s 237.1` IF
        `it is a financial interest in the ordinary meaning of the words`
    OR  CONSIDER kind
        WHEN `a security (s 237.1 "financial interest" (a))` THEN TRUE
        WHEN `a title to or an interest in capital, assets, property, profits, earnings or royalties (s 237.1 "financial interest" (b))` THEN TRUE
        WHEN `an option or other interest in, or a subscription to, a security (s 237.1 "financial interest" (c))` THEN TRUE
        WHEN `an agreement valuing the purchaser's interest by reference to a proportionate interest in a specified portfolio of assets (s 237.1 "financial interest" (d))` THEN TRUE
        WHEN `an agreement that money received will be repaid or treated as a subscription at the option of any person or the corporation (s 237.1 "financial interest" (e))` THEN TRUE
        WHEN `a profit-sharing agreement or certificate (s 237.1 "financial interest" (f))` THEN TRUE
        WHEN `a lease, claim or royalty in oil, natural gas or mining, or an interest in it (s 237.1 "financial interest" (g))` THEN TRUE
        WHEN `an income or annuity contract (s 237.1 "financial interest" (h))` THEN (NOT `the income or annuity contract was issued by an insurance company governed by an Act of Parliament or a law of a province`)
        WHEN `an investment contract (s 237.1 "financial interest" (i))` THEN TRUE
        WHEN `anything prescribed to be a financial interest (s 237.1 "financial interest" (j))` THEN `it is prescribed by the regulations to be a financial interest`
        WHEN `none of these kinds of financial interest (s 237.1)` THEN FALSE

-- src:2950 | financial loss means a financial loss arising out of an error, omission or misstatement in financial information concerning a corporation that is required under this Act or the regulations. (perte financière)
@ref CBCA s 237.1 "financial loss" (src:2950)
GIVEN `it is a financial loss` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it arose out of an error, omission or misstatement in financial information concerning a corporation` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the financial information is required under this Act or the regulations` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `financial loss within s 237.1` IF
        `it is a financial loss`
    AND `it arose out of an error, omission or misstatement in financial information concerning a corporation`
    AND `the financial information is required under this Act or the regulations`

-- "Includes any subsequent party that is joined in proceedings before a court": the ordinary meaning of
-- a third party, or a party joined later.
-- src:2951 | third party includes any subsequent party that is joined in proceedings before a court. (Version anglaise seulement)
@ref CBCA s 237.1 "third party" (src:2951)
GIVEN `it is a third party in the ordinary meaning of the words` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is a subsequent party joined in proceedings before a court` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `third party within s 237.1` IF
        `it is a third party in the ordinary meaning of the words`
    OR  `it is a subsequent party joined in proceedings before a court`

§§ `s 237.2 -- application of the part`

-- Both conditions: damages awarded to a plaintiff for financial loss, and more than one defendant or
-- third party found responsible for it.
-- src:2953 | 237.2 (1) This Part applies to the apportionment of damages awarded to a plaintiff for financial loss after a court has found more than one defendant or third party responsible for the financial loss.
@ref CBCA s 237.2(1) (src:2953)
GIVEN `damages are awarded to a plaintiff for financial loss` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the number of defendants and third parties the court has found responsible for the financial loss` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Part XIX.1 applies to the apportionment within s 237.2(1)` IF
        `damages are awarded to a plaintiff for financial loss`
    AND `the number of defendants and third parties the court has found responsible for the financial loss` GREATER THAN 1

-- The four excluded kinds of plaintiff. (b) is itself qualified: an agent of the Crown, a Crown
-- corporation or a government agency is excluded "unless a substantial part of its activities involves
-- trading ... in securities or other financial instruments". Whether a charity is one "within the meaning
-- of subsection 149.1(1) of the Income Tax Act" is taken as the kind itself: that Act is not among the sources.
-- src:2955 | (2) This Part does not apply to an award of damages to any of the following plaintiffs:
-- src:2956 | (a) Her Majesty in right of Canada or of a province;
-- src:2957 | (b) an agent of Her Majesty in right of Canada or of a province or a federal or provincial Crown corporation or government agency, unless a substantial part of its activities involves trading, including making investments in, securities or other financial instruments;
-- src:2958 | (c) a charitable organization, private foundation or public foundation within the meaning of subsection 149.1(1) of the Income Tax Act; or
-- src:2959 | (d) an unsecured creditor in respect of goods or services that the creditor provided to a corporation.
@ref CBCA s 237.2(2) (src:2955-2959)
DECLARE `Kind of plaintiff (s 237.2(2))` IS ONE OF
    `Her Majesty in right of Canada or of a province (s 237.2(2)(a))`
    `an agent of Her Majesty, a Crown corporation or a government agency (s 237.2(2)(b))`
    `a charitable organization, private foundation or public foundation (s 237.2(2)(c))`
    `an unsecured creditor in respect of goods or services provided to a corporation (s 237.2(2)(d))`
    `any other plaintiff (s 237.2(2))`

-- src:2955 | (2) This Part does not apply to an award of damages to any of the following plaintiffs:
-- src:2956 | (a) Her Majesty in right of Canada or of a province;
-- src:2957 | (b) an agent of Her Majesty in right of Canada or of a province or a federal or provincial Crown corporation or government agency, unless a substantial part of its activities involves trading, including making investments in, securities or other financial instruments;
-- src:2958 | (c) a charitable organization, private foundation or public foundation within the meaning of subsection 149.1(1) of the Income Tax Act; or
-- src:2959 | (d) an unsecured creditor in respect of goods or services that the creditor provided to a corporation.
@ref CBCA s 237.2(2) (src:2955-2959)
GIVEN kind IS A `Kind of plaintiff (s 237.2(2))`
      `a substantial part of the activities of the plaintiff involves trading, including making investments in, securities or other financial instruments` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Part XIX.1 does not apply to the plaintiff within s 237.2(2)` IF
    CONSIDER kind
    WHEN `Her Majesty in right of Canada or of a province (s 237.2(2)(a))` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `an agent of Her Majesty, a Crown corporation or a government agency (s 237.2(2)(b))` THEN (NOT `a substantial part of the activities of the plaintiff involves trading, including making investments in, securities or other financial instruments`)
    WHEN `a charitable organization, private foundation or public foundation (s 237.2(2)(c))` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `an unsecured creditor in respect of goods or services provided to a corporation (s 237.2(2)(d))` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `any other plaintiff (s 237.2(2))` THEN FALSE

§§ `s 237.3 -- apportionment by degree of responsibility`

-- "Liable ... only for the portion of the damages that corresponds to their degree of responsibility".
-- "Subject to this section and sections 237.4 to 237.6": the exceptions are in the rules for those sections
-- and are brought together in `the basis of liability` below.
-- src:2963 | 237.3 (1) Subject to this section and sections 237.4 to 237.6, every defendant or third party who has been found responsible for a financial loss is liable to the plaintiff only for the portion of the damages that corresponds to their degree of responsibility for the loss.
@ref CBCA s 237.3(1) (src:2963)
GIVEN `the damages awarded in dollars` IS A NUMBER
      `fraction of the responsibility for the loss borne by the defendant or third party` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the portion of the damages for which a defendant or third party is liable within s 237.3(1)` IS
    `the damages awarded in dollars` TIMES `fraction of the responsibility for the loss borne by the defendant or third party`

-- The time limit: "within one year after the date that the judgment was made enforceable". The counting
-- of the year is the core convention (fork F1 in the keel's notes): the day the judgment was made
-- enforceable is day 0 and the anniversary is in time.
-- src:2965 | (2) If any part of the damages awarded against a responsible defendant or third party is uncollectable, the court may, on the application of the plaintiff, reallocate that amount to the other responsible defendants or third parties, if the application is made within one year after the date that the judgment was made enforceable.
@ref CBCA s 237.3(2) (src:2965)
GIVETH A `Time limit`
`the period for the plaintiff to apply to reallocate within s 237.3(2)` MEANS
    `Time limit` WITH
        `number of units` IS 1
        `unit of time` IS `calendar years`

-- src:2965 | (2) If any part of the damages awarded against a responsible defendant or third party is uncollectable, the court may, on the application of the plaintiff, reallocate that amount to the other responsible defendants or third parties, if the application is made within one year after the date that the judgment was made enforceable.
@ref CBCA s 237.3(2) (src:2965)
GIVEN `the date the judgment was made enforceable` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
DECIDE `the last day to apply to reallocate an uncollectable amount within s 237.3(2)` IS
    `the last day of` `the period for the plaintiff to apply to reallocate within s 237.3(2)` `counted from` `the date the judgment was made enforceable`

-- The court "may" reallocate: the permission is open when part of the damages is uncollectable, the
-- plaintiff applies and the application is in time. The court's decision to do so is its own.
-- src:2965 | (2) If any part of the damages awarded against a responsible defendant or third party is uncollectable, the court may, on the application of the plaintiff, reallocate that amount to the other responsible defendants or third parties, if the application is made within one year after the date that the judgment was made enforceable.
@ref CBCA s 237.3(2) (src:2965)
GIVEN `part of the damages awarded against a responsible defendant or third party is uncollectable` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the plaintiff has applied for the reallocation` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the date the judgment was made enforceable` IS A DATE
      `the date of the application` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the court may reallocate the uncollectable amount within s 237.3(2)` IF
        `part of the damages awarded against a responsible defendant or third party is uncollectable`
    AND `the plaintiff has applied for the reallocation`
    AND `done within the time limit` `the period for the plaintiff to apply to reallocate within s 237.3(2)` `the date the judgment was made enforceable` `the date of the application`

-- src:2967 | (3) The amount that may be reallocated to each of the other responsible defendants or third parties under subsection (2) is calculated by multiplying the uncollectable amount by the percentage that corresponds to the degree of responsibility of that defendant or third party for the total financial loss.
@ref CBCA s 237.3(3) (src:2967)
GIVEN `the uncollectable amount in dollars` IS A NUMBER
      `fraction of the responsibility of the other defendant or third party for the total financial loss` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the amount that may be reallocated to the other defendant or third party within s 237.3(3)` IS
    `the uncollectable amount in dollars` TIMES `fraction of the responsibility of the other defendant or third party for the total financial loss`

-- "May not be more than fifty per cent of the amount originally awarded": a ceiling on the amount
-- worked out under subsection (3); exactly fifty per cent is allowed.
-- src:2969 | (4) The maximum amount determined under subsection (3), in respect of any responsible defendant or third party, may not be more than fifty per cent of the amount originally awarded against that responsible defendant or third party.
@ref CBCA s 237.3(4) (src:2969)
GIVEN `the amount determined under subsection 237.3(3) in dollars` IS A NUMBER
      `the amount originally awarded against that defendant or third party in dollars` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the most that may be reallocated to that defendant or third party within s 237.3(4)` IS
    IF `the amount determined under subsection 237.3(3) in dollars` GREATER THAN `the amount originally awarded against that defendant or third party in dollars` TIMES (50%)
    THEN `the amount originally awarded against that defendant or third party in dollars` TIMES (50%)
    ELSE `the amount determined under subsection 237.3(3) in dollars`

§§ `s 237.4 -- exception: fraud`

-- The plaintiff may recover the whole of the damages awarded from a defendant or third party held
-- responsible if it was established that they acted fraudulently or dishonestly.
-- src:2971 | 237.4 (1) The plaintiff may recover the whole amount of the damages awarded by the court from any defendant or third party who has been held responsible for a financial loss if it was established that the defendant or third party acted fraudulently or dishonestly.
@ref CBCA s 237.4(1) (src:2971)
GIVEN `the defendant or third party has been held responsible for the financial loss` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it was established that the defendant or third party acted fraudulently or dishonestly` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the plaintiff may recover the whole amount of the damages from the defendant or third party within s 237.4(1)` IF
        `the defendant or third party has been held responsible for the financial loss`
    AND `it was established that the defendant or third party acted fraudulently or dishonestly`

-- Hohfeld: the right to claim contribution is the fraudulent defendant's; the liability to it is the
-- other defendant's or third party's, who "is held responsible for the loss".
-- src:2973 | (2) The defendant or third party referred to in subsection (1) is entitled to claim contribution from any other defendant or third party who is held responsible for the loss.
@ref CBCA s 237.4(2) (src:2973)
GIVEN `the person is the defendant or third party referred to in subsection 237.4(1)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the other defendant or third party is held responsible for the loss` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the defendant or third party is entitled to claim contribution within s 237.4(2)` IF
        `the person is the defendant or third party referred to in subsection 237.4(1)`
    AND `the other defendant or third party is held responsible for the loss`

§§ `s 237.5 -- joint and several, or solidary, liability`

-- (2)(a): a personal body corporate is one that is not actively engaged in a financial, commercial or
-- industrial business AND is controlled by an individual or by a group of individuals connected in the
-- ways listed. Control is taken as a fact (the keel's rules for control work from holdings; this definition
-- is satisfied by the controller being an individual or a family).
-- src:2984 | (a) a personal body corporate is a body corporate that is not actively engaged in any financial, commercial or industrial business and that is controlled by an individual, or by a group of individuals who are connected by marriage, common-law partnership or any legal parent-child relationship or are connected indirectly by a combination of those relationships, whether or not the individuals through whom they are connected are members of the group; and
@ref CBCA s 237.5(2)(a) (src:2984)
GIVEN `the body corporate is not actively engaged in any financial, commercial or industrial business` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the body corporate is controlled by an individual` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the body corporate is controlled by a group of individuals connected by marriage, common-law partnership or any legal parent-child relationship, or connected indirectly by a combination of those relationships` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `personal body corporate within s 237.5(2)(a)` IF
        `the body corporate is not actively engaged in any financial, commercial or industrial business`
    AND (    `the body corporate is controlled by an individual`
         OR  `the body corporate is controlled by a group of individuals connected by marriage, common-law partnership or any legal parent-child relationship, or connected indirectly by a combination of those relationships`)

-- src:2985 | (b) a common-law partnership is a relationship between two persons who are cohabiting with each other in a conjugal relationship and have done so for a period of at least one year.
@ref CBCA s 237.5(2)(b) (src:2985)
GIVEN `the two persons are cohabiting with each other in a conjugal relationship` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the number of years the two persons have cohabited` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `common-law partnership within s 237.5(2)(b)` IF
        `the two persons are cohabiting with each other in a conjugal relationship`
    AND `the number of years the two persons have cohabited` AT LEAST 1

-- The plaintiff's holding on one day: whether an interest was acquired that day, and the value, in
-- dollars, of the plaintiff's total financial interest in the corporation at the close of business.
-- src:2978 | (a) had a financial interest in a corporation on the day that an error, omission or misstatement in financial information concerning the corporation occurred, or acquired a financial interest in the period between the day that the error, omission or misstatement occurred and the day, as determined by the court, that it was generally disclosed; and
-- src:2979 | (b) has established that the value of the plaintiff’s total financial interest in the corporation was not more than the prescribed amount at the close of business on the day that the error, omission or misstatement occurred or at the close of business on any day that the plaintiff acquired a financial interest in the period referred to in paragraph (a).
@ref CBCA s 237.5(1) (src:2978-2979)
DECLARE `Close of business position of a plaintiff (s 237.5(1))` HAS
    `the day` IS A DATE
    `the plaintiff acquired a financial interest on that day` IS A BOOLEAN
    `value of the plaintiff's total financial interest in the corporation in dollars` IS A NUMBER

-- A day on which the plaintiff acquired a financial interest "in the period between" the day of the
-- error and the day it was generally disclosed (as determined by the court). Both ends are read as in
-- the period (fork F-237.5-1 in NOTES.md).
-- src:2978 | (a) had a financial interest in a corporation on the day that an error, omission or misstatement in financial information concerning the corporation occurred, or acquired a financial interest in the period between the day that the error, omission or misstatement occurred and the day, as determined by the court, that it was generally disclosed; and
@ref CBCA s 237.5(1)(a) (src:2978)
GIVEN position IS A `Close of business position of a plaintiff (s 237.5(1))`
      `the day the error, omission or misstatement occurred` IS A DATE
      `the day it was generally disclosed, as determined by the court` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the position is an acquisition in the period within s 237.5(1)(a)` IF
        position's `the plaintiff acquired a financial interest on that day`
    AND position's `the day` AT LEAST `the day the error, omission or misstatement occurred`
    AND position's `the day` AT MOST `the day it was generally disclosed, as determined by the court`

-- src:2978 | (a) had a financial interest in a corporation on the day that an error, omission or misstatement in financial information concerning the corporation occurred, or acquired a financial interest in the period between the day that the error, omission or misstatement occurred and the day, as determined by the court, that it was generally disclosed; and
@ref CBCA s 237.5(1)(a) (src:2978)
GIVEN `the plaintiff had a financial interest in the corporation on the day the error, omission or misstatement occurred` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day the error, omission or misstatement occurred` IS A DATE
      `the day it was generally disclosed, as determined by the court` IS A DATE
      positions IS A LIST OF `Close of business position of a plaintiff (s 237.5(1))`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the plaintiff had or acquired a financial interest in time within s 237.5(1)(a)` IF
        `the plaintiff had a financial interest in the corporation on the day the error, omission or misstatement occurred`
    OR  any (GIVEN p YIELD `the position is an acquisition in the period within s 237.5(1)(a)` p `the day the error, omission or misstatement occurred` `the day it was generally disclosed, as determined by the court`) positions

-- src:2979 | (b) has established that the value of the plaintiff’s total financial interest in the corporation was not more than the prescribed amount at the close of business on the day that the error, omission or misstatement occurred or at the close of business on any day that the plaintiff acquired a financial interest in the period referred to in paragraph (a).
@ref CBCA s 237.5(1)(b) (src:2979)
GIVEN position IS A `Close of business position of a plaintiff (s 237.5(1))`
      `the day the error, omission or misstatement occurred` IS A DATE
      `the day it was generally disclosed, as determined by the court` IS A DATE
      `the prescribed amount in dollars` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the position is an acquisition in the period within the prescribed amount within s 237.5(1)(b)` IF
        `the position is an acquisition in the period within s 237.5(1)(a)` position `the day the error, omission or misstatement occurred` `the day it was generally disclosed, as determined by the court`
    AND position's `value of the plaintiff's total financial interest in the corporation in dollars` AT MOST `the prescribed amount in dollars`

-- "Not more than the prescribed amount": a value equal to the amount qualifies. The plaintiff must have
-- "established" the value, so that is a fact beside the figures.
-- src:2979 | (b) has established that the value of the plaintiff’s total financial interest in the corporation was not more than the prescribed amount at the close of business on the day that the error, omission or misstatement occurred or at the close of business on any day that the plaintiff acquired a financial interest in the period referred to in paragraph (a).
@ref CBCA s 237.5(1)(b) (src:2979)
GIVEN `the plaintiff has established the value of the total financial interest` IS A BOOLEAN
      `value of the plaintiff's total financial interest in the corporation on the day the error, omission or misstatement occurred in dollars` IS A NUMBER
      `the day the error, omission or misstatement occurred` IS A DATE
      `the day it was generally disclosed, as determined by the court` IS A DATE
      positions IS A LIST OF `Close of business position of a plaintiff (s 237.5(1))`
      `the prescribed amount in dollars` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the value of the total financial interest was within the prescribed amount within s 237.5(1)(b)` IF
        `the plaintiff has established the value of the total financial interest`
    AND (    `value of the plaintiff's total financial interest in the corporation on the day the error, omission or misstatement occurred in dollars` AT MOST `the prescribed amount in dollars`
         OR  any (GIVEN p YIELD `the position is an acquisition in the period within the prescribed amount within s 237.5(1)(b)` p `the day the error, omission or misstatement occurred` `the day it was generally disclosed, as determined by the court` `the prescribed amount in dollars`) positions)

-- (1.1): the exception. Either way of bringing the action takes the plaintiff out of subsection (1).
-- src:2981 | (1.1) Subsection (1) does not apply when the plaintiff brings the action as a member of a partnership or other association or as a trustee in bankruptcy, liquidator, receiver or sequestrator of a body corporate.
@ref CBCA s 237.5(1.1) (src:2981)
GIVEN `the plaintiff brings the action as a member of a partnership or other association` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the plaintiff brings the action as a trustee in bankruptcy, liquidator, receiver or sequestrator of a body corporate` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `subsection 237.5(1) does not apply to the plaintiff within s 237.5(1.1)` IF
        `the plaintiff brings the action as a member of a partnership or other association`
    OR  `the plaintiff brings the action as a trustee in bankruptcy, liquidator, receiver or sequestrator of a body corporate`

-- The whole of subsection (1): the defendants and third parties referred to in subsection 237.2(1) are
-- jointly and severally liable to a plaintiff who is an individual or a personal body corporate and
-- meets (a) AND (b), unless subsection (1.1) takes the plaintiff out.
-- src:2977 | 237.5 (1) Defendants and third parties referred to in subsection 237.2(1) are jointly and severally, or solidarily, liable for the damages awarded to a plaintiff who is an individual or a personal body corporate and who
-- src:2978 | (a) had a financial interest in a corporation on the day that an error, omission or misstatement in financial information concerning the corporation occurred, or acquired a financial interest in the period between the day that the error, omission or misstatement occurred and the day, as determined by the court, that it was generally disclosed; and
-- src:2979 | (b) has established that the value of the plaintiff’s total financial interest in the corporation was not more than the prescribed amount at the close of business on the day that the error, omission or misstatement occurred or at the close of business on any day that the plaintiff acquired a financial interest in the period referred to in paragraph (a).
@ref CBCA s 237.5(1) (src:2977-2979)
GIVEN `the defendants and third parties are those referred to in subsection 237.2(1)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the plaintiff is an individual` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the plaintiff is a personal body corporate` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the plaintiff had a financial interest in the corporation on the day the error, omission or misstatement occurred` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day the error, omission or misstatement occurred` IS A DATE
      `the day it was generally disclosed, as determined by the court` IS A DATE
      positions IS A LIST OF `Close of business position of a plaintiff (s 237.5(1))`
      `the plaintiff has established the value of the total financial interest` IS A BOOLEAN
      `value of the plaintiff's total financial interest in the corporation on the day the error, omission or misstatement occurred in dollars` IS A NUMBER
      `the prescribed amount in dollars` IS A NUMBER
      `subsection 237.5(1) does not apply to the plaintiff because of subsection 237.5(1.1)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the defendants and third parties are jointly and severally liable within s 237.5(1)` IF
        `the defendants and third parties are those referred to in subsection 237.2(1)`
    AND (    `the plaintiff is an individual`
         OR  `the plaintiff is a personal body corporate`)
    AND `the plaintiff had or acquired a financial interest in time within s 237.5(1)(a)` `the plaintiff had a financial interest in the corporation on the day the error, omission or misstatement occurred` `the day the error, omission or misstatement occurred` `the day it was generally disclosed, as determined by the court` positions
    AND `the value of the total financial interest was within the prescribed amount within s 237.5(1)(b)` `the plaintiff has established the value of the total financial interest` `value of the plaintiff's total financial interest in the corporation on the day the error, omission or misstatement occurred in dollars` `the day the error, omission or misstatement occurred` `the day it was generally disclosed, as determined by the court` positions `the prescribed amount in dollars`
    AND (NOT `subsection 237.5(1) does not apply to the plaintiff because of subsection 237.5(1.1)`)

§§ `s 237.6 -- equitable grounds`

-- Above the prescribed amount, the court may nevertheless hold the defendants and third parties jointly
-- and severally liable if it considers it just and reasonable. At or below the amount, subsection
-- 237.5(1)(b) is met, so this power is not needed; it is open only above the amount.
-- src:2987 | 237.6 (1) If the value of the plaintiff’s total financial interest referred to in subsection 237.5(1) is greater than the prescribed amount, a court may nevertheless determine that the defendants and third parties are jointly and severally, or solidarily, liable if the court considers that it is just and reasonable to do so.
@ref CBCA s 237.6(1) (src:2987)
GIVEN `the value of the plaintiff's total financial interest in dollars` IS A NUMBER
      `the prescribed amount in dollars` IS A NUMBER
      `the court considers that it is just and reasonable to hold the defendants and third parties jointly and severally liable` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the court may hold the defendants and third parties jointly and severally liable within s 237.6(1)` IF
        `the value of the plaintiff's total financial interest in dollars` GREATER THAN `the prescribed amount in dollars`
    AND `the court considers that it is just and reasonable to hold the defendants and third parties jointly and severally liable`

§§ `s 237.7 -- value of a security`

-- (4) "organized market": a recognized exchange for a class of securities, or a market that regularly
-- publishes the price of that class in a publication generally available to the public.
-- src:3002 | (4) In this section, organized market means a recognized exchange for a class of securities or a market that regularly publishes the price of that class of securities in a publication that is generally available to the public.
@ref CBCA s 237.7(4) (src:3002)
GIVEN `it is a recognized exchange for a class of securities` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is a market that regularly publishes the price of that class of securities in a publication generally available to the public` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `organized market within s 237.7(4)` IF
        `it is a recognized exchange for a class of securities`
    OR  `it is a market that regularly publishes the price of that class of securities in a publication generally available to the public`

-- The mean of two prices, where both are given; (b) and (c) of subsection (1) both say "the average".
-- src:2995 | (b) if no closing price is given, the average of the highest and lowest prices of that class of security; or
-- src:2996 | (c) if the security was not traded, the average of the bid and ask prices of that class of security.
@ref CBCA s 237.7(1)(b), s 237.7(1)(c) helper (src:2995-2996)
GIVEN `the first price in dollars` IS A MAYBE NUMBER
      `the second price in dollars` IS A MAYBE NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `the average of two prices` IS
    CONSIDER `the first price in dollars`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
    WHEN JUST x THEN CONSIDER `the second price in dollars`
                     WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
                     WHEN JUST y THEN JUST ((x PLUS y) DIVIDED BY 2)

-- The order of the three limbs is the text's: (a) the closing price; (b) if no closing price is given, the
-- average of the highest and lowest prices; (c) if the security was not traded, the average of the bid and
-- ask prices. A traded security with no closing price falls to (b); a security that was not traded has no
-- highest and lowest price, so it falls to (c) (fork F-237.7-1 in NOTES.md). Where the figures the limb
-- needs are not given, the answer is NOTHING (not covered), never 0. Outside an organized market the
-- answer is NOTHING too: s 237.8(1) has the court determine the value there.
-- src:2993 | 237.7 (1) When, in order to establish the value of the total financial interest referred to in subsection 237.5(1), it is necessary to determine the value of a security that is traded on an organized market, the value of the security is, on the day specified in subsection (3),
-- src:2994 | (a) the closing price of that class of security;
-- src:2995 | (b) if no closing price is given, the average of the highest and lowest prices of that class of security; or
-- src:2996 | (c) if the security was not traded, the average of the bid and ask prices of that class of security.
@ref CBCA s 237.7(1) (src:2993-2996)
GIVEN `the security is traded on an organized market` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the closing price of that class of security in dollars` IS A MAYBE NUMBER
      `the highest price of that class of security in dollars` IS A MAYBE NUMBER
      `the lowest price of that class of security in dollars` IS A MAYBE NUMBER
      `the security was traded on the day` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the bid price of that class of security in dollars` IS A MAYBE NUMBER
      `the ask price of that class of security in dollars` IS A MAYBE NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `the value of the security within s 237.7(1)` IS
    IF NOT `the security is traded on an organized market`
    THEN NOTHING
    ELSE CONSIDER `the closing price of that class of security in dollars`
         WHEN JUST c THEN JUST c
         WHEN NOTHING THEN IF `the security was traded on the day`
                           THEN `the average of two prices` `the highest price of that class of security in dollars` `the lowest price of that class of security in dollars`
                           ELSE `the average of two prices` `the bid price of that class of security in dollars` `the ask price of that class of security in dollars`

-- src:2998 | (2) The court may adjust the value of a security that has been determined under subsection (1) when the court considers it reasonable to do so.
@ref CBCA s 237.7(2) (src:2998)
GIVEN `the court considers it reasonable to adjust the value` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the court may adjust the value within s 237.7(2)` IF
    `the court considers it reasonable to adjust the value`

-- (3): the value is fixed as of the day of the error, unless the security was acquired in the period
-- between that day and the day of general disclosure, when it is fixed as of the day it was acquired.
-- src:3000 | (3) The value of the security is to be determined as of the day that the error, omission or misstatement occurred. If the security was acquired in the period between that day and the day, as determined by the court, that the error, omission or misstatement was generally disclosed, the value is to be determined as of the day that it was acquired.
@ref CBCA s 237.7(3) (src:3000)
GIVEN `the day the error, omission or misstatement occurred` IS A DATE
      `the day it was generally disclosed, as determined by the court` IS A DATE
      `the day the security was acquired` IS A MAYBE DATE
GIVETH A DATE
DECIDE `the day as of which the value is determined within s 237.7(3)` IS
    CONSIDER `the day the security was acquired`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN `the day the error, omission or misstatement occurred`
    WHEN JUST d THEN IF d AT LEAST `the day the error, omission or misstatement occurred` AND d AT MOST `the day it was generally disclosed, as determined by the court`
                     THEN d
                     ELSE `the day the error, omission or misstatement occurred`

§§ `s 237.8 -- other financial interests`

-- "The court shall determine the value" where the interest is subject to resale restrictions or there is no
-- organized market: either condition is enough ("or").
-- src:3004 | 237.8 (1) The court shall determine the value of all or any part of a financial interest that is subject to resale restrictions or for which there is no organized market.
@ref CBCA s 237.8(1) (src:3004)
GIVEN `the financial interest is subject to resale restrictions` IS A BOOLEAN
      `there is no organized market for the financial interest` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the court must determine the value within s 237.8(1)` IF
        `the financial interest is subject to resale restrictions`
    OR  `there is no organized market for the financial interest`

§§ `s 237.9 -- application to determine value`

-- "At any time before or during the course of the proceedings": the application is in time unless the
-- proceedings are over.
-- src:3010 | 237.9 The plaintiff may, by application made at any time before or during the course of the proceedings, request the court to determine the value of the plaintiff’s financial interest for the purpose of subsection 237.5(1).
@ref CBCA s 237.9 (src:3010)
GIVEN `the application is made before or during the course of the proceedings` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the plaintiff may apply for the court to determine the value of the financial interest within s 237.9` IF
    `the application is made before or during the course of the proceedings`

§§ `The basis on which a defendant or third party is liable -- s 237.3(1), s 237.4(1), s 237.5(1), s 237.6(1)`

-- The four provisions say, in turn, that liability is proportionate to responsibility (237.3(1), "subject
-- to this section and sections 237.4 to 237.6"), that a fraudulent or dishonest defendant is liable for the
-- whole (237.4(1)), and that defendants are jointly and severally liable under 237.5(1) or, on equitable
-- grounds, 237.6(1). This rule only puts the three exceptions in front of the general rule.
-- src:2963 | 237.3 (1) Subject to this section and sections 237.4 to 237.6, every defendant or third party who has been found responsible for a financial loss is liable to the plaintiff only for the portion of the damages that corresponds to their degree of responsibility for the loss.
-- src:2971 | 237.4 (1) The plaintiff may recover the whole amount of the damages awarded by the court from any defendant or third party who has been held responsible for a financial loss if it was established that the defendant or third party acted fraudulently or dishonestly.
-- src:2977 | 237.5 (1) Defendants and third parties referred to in subsection 237.2(1) are jointly and severally, or solidarily, liable for the damages awarded to a plaintiff who is an individual or a personal body corporate and who
-- src:2987 | 237.6 (1) If the value of the plaintiff’s total financial interest referred to in subsection 237.5(1) is greater than the prescribed amount, a court may nevertheless determine that the defendants and third parties are jointly and severally, or solidarily, liable if the court considers that it is just and reasonable to do so.
@ref CBCA s 237.3(1), s 237.4(1), s 237.5(1), s 237.6(1) (src:2963 src:2971 src:2977 src:2987)
DECLARE `Basis of the liability of a defendant or third party (Part XIX.1)` IS ONE OF
    `liable only for the portion of the damages that corresponds to their degree of responsibility`
    `liable for the whole amount of the damages awarded because they acted fraudulently or dishonestly`
    `jointly and severally, or solidarily, liable for the damages awarded`

-- src:2963 | 237.3 (1) Subject to this section and sections 237.4 to 237.6, every defendant or third party who has been found responsible for a financial loss is liable to the plaintiff only for the portion of the damages that corresponds to their degree of responsibility for the loss.
-- src:2971 | 237.4 (1) The plaintiff may recover the whole amount of the damages awarded by the court from any defendant or third party who has been held responsible for a financial loss if it was established that the defendant or third party acted fraudulently or dishonestly.
-- src:2977 | 237.5 (1) Defendants and third parties referred to in subsection 237.2(1) are jointly and severally, or solidarily, liable for the damages awarded to a plaintiff who is an individual or a personal body corporate and who
-- src:2987 | 237.6 (1) If the value of the plaintiff’s total financial interest referred to in subsection 237.5(1) is greater than the prescribed amount, a court may nevertheless determine that the defendants and third parties are jointly and severally, or solidarily, liable if the court considers that it is just and reasonable to do so.
@ref CBCA s 237.3(1), s 237.4(1), s 237.5(1), s 237.6(1) (src:2963 src:2971 src:2977 src:2987)
GIVEN `the plaintiff may recover the whole amount from the defendant or third party under subsection 237.4(1)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the defendants and third parties are jointly and severally liable under subsection 237.5(1)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the court has held the defendants and third parties jointly and severally liable under subsection 237.6(1)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Basis of the liability of a defendant or third party (Part XIX.1)`
DECIDE `the basis of the liability within s 237.3(1) and s 237.4 to s 237.6` IS
    BRANCH IF `the plaintiff may recover the whole amount from the defendant or third party under subsection 237.4(1)`
           THEN `liable for the whole amount of the damages awarded because they acted fraudulently or dishonestly`
           IF `the defendants and third parties are jointly and severally liable under subsection 237.5(1)`
           THEN `jointly and severally, or solidarily, liable for the damages awarded`
           IF `the court has held the defendants and third parties jointly and severally liable under subsection 237.6(1)`
           THEN `jointly and severally, or solidarily, liable for the damages awarded`
           OTHERWISE `liable only for the portion of the damages that corresponds to their degree of responsibility`
